WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.940
Series super Applied Geometry. season one episode one. Have you ever wondered why the world around us looks the way it does?

00:09.100 --> 00:14.240
Geometry the branch of mathematics that concerns shapes and their properties is a key player

00:14.560 --> 00:21.560
It's not just about abstract concepts and complicated figures. It's deeply woven into the fabric of our daily lives

00:22.080 --> 00:24.080
Consider the layout of city streets

00:24.080 --> 00:27.640
It's meticulously planned on grids and angles to maximize efficiency

00:28.360 --> 00:35.800
The design of our homes from the rectangular shape of bricks to the triangular trusses in our roofs is all about geometry

00:35.800 --> 00:41.680
It's there in the perfect circle of your morning coffee cup the rectangular screen of your smartphone

00:41.880 --> 00:44.480
Even the hexagonal pattern of a honeycomb

00:45.160 --> 00:51.640
Geometry isn't confined to the classroom. It's a silent architect shaping our world in ways. We often take for granted

00:51.880 --> 00:59.160
It's not just about triangles squares or circles. It's about how these shapes interact and combine to create our reality

00:59.200 --> 01:05.840
So geometry is not just about boring theorems. It's everywhere around us. How does your smartphone know which way is up?

01:06.000 --> 01:09.480
This isn't magic. It's geometry at work in technology

01:09.960 --> 01:17.400
Inside your devices tiny sensors called accelerometers and gyroscopes are constantly measuring forces and rotations

01:17.640 --> 01:21.880
They use geometric principles to translate physical movement into digital information

01:22.560 --> 01:26.760
Telling your phone whether it's upright on its side or upside down

01:27.160 --> 01:34.460
But it's not just about orientation ever wondered how your GPS knows exactly where you are. That's geometry, too

01:34.960 --> 01:41.480
GPS systems work by receiving signals from multiple satellites and using the time it takes for each signal to arrive

01:41.760 --> 01:48.720
By applying geometric calculations to these times the GPS can pinpoint your exact location on the earth's surface

01:48.720 --> 01:52.960
So next time you pull out your phone to find your way or flip your screen remember

01:53.080 --> 02:00.640
There's a lot of complex geometry happening behind the scenes without geometry our gadgets would be a lot less smart

02:00.880 --> 02:05.800
Why do bees build hexagonal honeycombs you may ask? Well, it's all about efficiency

02:06.520 --> 02:12.080
Bees have figured out that hexagons are the shape that best allows them to maximize their storage space

02:12.560 --> 02:18.000
While using the least amount of wax it's a brilliant example of geometry in nature

02:18.120 --> 02:22.420
But bees aren't the only ones playing with shapes take a look at a sunflower

02:22.840 --> 02:26.200
Notice the spiral patterns those aren't just for show each

02:26.640 --> 02:33.480
Floret is positioned at a specific angle to ensure that as many seeds as possible can be packed into the flower head

02:33.640 --> 02:37.240
This angle known as the golden angle is approximately

02:38.120 --> 02:42.160
137.5 degrees and it's not just bees and sunflowers

02:42.800 --> 02:47.960
From the radial symmetry of a starfish to the intricate structure of a snowflake

02:48.780 --> 02:51.960
Geometric shapes and patterns are everywhere in the natural world

02:52.600 --> 03:00.760
It's a testament to how nature has been playing with geometry for millions of years ever noticed the symmetry in a beautiful piece of art

03:01.600 --> 03:07.040
Geometry is the unsung hero in the world of art and design shaping the elegance

03:07.040 --> 03:09.680
We admire and the functionality we rely on

03:10.360 --> 03:16.240
Artists like architects of imagination employ geometric shapes to orchestrate balance and harmony in their works

03:16.520 --> 03:24.600
They weave circles triangles and squares into a visual symphony that captivates our senses and stirs our emotions

03:25.280 --> 03:30.400
Meanwhile in the realm of design geometry is the cornerstone of practical aesthetics

03:31.040 --> 03:38.080
Designers use geometric principles to marry form with function creating products that are not only visually appealing

03:38.080 --> 03:44.320
But also intuitive and efficient from the sleek lines of a smartphone to the ergonomic curves of a chair

03:44.560 --> 03:47.640
Geometry is instrumental in shaping our everyday experiences

03:47.800 --> 03:52.920
So the next time you marvel at a masterpiece or appreciate a well-designed product remember this

03:53.240 --> 04:00.360
Art and design are more than just creativity their geometry in action. So why should we care about geometry?

04:00.800 --> 04:06.240
Well, it's quite simple really geometry is everywhere in every nook and cranny of our daily lives

04:06.240 --> 04:09.080
And it's been that way since the beginning of time

04:09.280 --> 04:17.280
It's in the vibrant patterns of the natural world from the spiral of a snail's shell to the intricate web spun by a spider

04:17.600 --> 04:24.720
It's in the technology we use from the sleek design of our smartphones to the ambitious blueprints of a skyscraper

04:25.240 --> 04:32.280
It's in the art we create from the harmonious proportions of a Renaissance painting to the bold lines of a modern sculpture

04:32.840 --> 04:39.520
Every day we're interacting with geometry often without even realizing it. It's more than just a subject

04:39.520 --> 04:40.600
We learn in school

04:40.600 --> 04:46.280
It's a fundamental part of our world a language that helps us understand and shape the world around us

04:46.480 --> 04:52.880
So next time you see a perfect circle or a right angle take a moment to appreciate the geometry at work

04:52.880 --> 04:59.200
Geometry is not just a subject in school. It's a way of understanding and shaping the world around us

